<title>USA: CME says no limit last two days of expiring hogs.</title>
<headline>CME says no limit last two days of expiring hogs.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange has notified participants in lean hog futures and options trading that there will be no daily limits the last two days of trading in the expiring contract.</p>
<p>February 1997 lean hogs will expire at 1200 CST/1800 GMT on Friday, February 14.</p>
<p>The February lean hog contract is the first of the new lean hog contracts to expire. All subsequent contracts will expire on the tenth business day of the month with no price limits the last two days of trading, the CME said in a clearing house advisory notice.</p>
<p>((Jerry Bieszk 312-408-8725))</p>
